\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This site-specific sculpture consists of two identical phalaenopsis orchids, one real and one artificial, presented side by side.\'a0 
\f0\i signs
\f1\i0  takes the ubiquitous interior design element of the moth orchid (found in minimalist kitchens, spa-bathrooms, hotel lobbies, and corporate offices the world over) and points to its paradoxical semiotic work invoking both simplicity and luxury at once.\'a0The doubling of the plant, pairing the one alive sourced in local flower markets with its polyester-and-plastic simulacrum from New York City, points to its specious duality as a sign.}